sequenceDiagram
    participant Setup as Setup / USB Provisioner
    participant Rails as Rails + PostgreSQL
    participant Sensor as Sensor Pico Package
    participant MQTT as Mosquitto
    participant Py as Python Controller
    participant Act as Dedicated Actuator Pico

    Setup->>Rails: POST provision_zone(package identity)
    Rails->>Rails: transaction: bind Zone + create ch0..ch3 + allocate global lines
    Rails-->>Setup: Zone ID and exact backend-issued channel IDs
    Setup->>Sensor: provision Zone, package, ch0..ch3, network settings
    Sensor-->>Setup: VG_PROVISION_OK with exact applied IDs
    Setup->>Rails: verify acknowledgement and retain backend topology authority

    Sensor->>MQTT: retained state for known Zone / Node
    MQTT-->>Rails: MQTT consumer delivers telemetry
    Rails->>Rails: reconcile known Node and persist reading plus last_seen_at
    Note over Rails: Unknown telemetry is diagnostic only and does not create production Nodes

    MQTT-->>Py: retained Node state + retained system config
    Py->>Py: evaluate Node crop, freshness, schedule, and installed capacity
    alt eligible automatic watering
        Py->>MQTT: non-retained Zone/Node actuator START
        MQTT->>Act: command from any Zone
        Act->>Act: validate global topology then journal before GPIO with local cutoff
        Act->>MQTT: status with originating Zone and Node
    else crop-less, unsupported, or unsafe
        Py->>MQTT: controller skip telemetry
    end
